No, cheating your way out of a DUI is not an advisable option. Not only can it result in further criminal charges, but it will also be detected in most cases, leaving you with a permanent criminal record. There are many more effective, less risky alternatives to consider, such as negotiating for a lesser charge or enrolling in a diversion program. Seeking professional help from a lawyer or an experienced driving under the influence specialist can also offer the best outcome in your case. 
